// src/v4/extdeps/formats/csv.dag
//
// Scope: CSV (Comma-Separated Values) data format model — direction-agnostic.
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180 (RFC 4180 — fixed edition)
//
// Owns:
//   - **RFC 4180 wire profile** for this L-2 artifact: COMMA-separated fields,
//     DQUOTE-quoted fields with doubled-DQUOTE escape (§2) — **not** a
//     tunable multi-dialect CSV surface here (TSV / custom separators = out of
//     scope for this authority file unless operator opens a sibling anchor).
//   - `CsvDialect` — nullary witness for that pinned profile (`CsvDialectRfc4180`).
//   - `CsvDocument` / `CsvRow` — honest **pre-ruling** carriers for tabular
//     CSV data: `width: Nat` + `List<String>` per row (see **RECTANGULARITY**
//     below). This is **not** yet the post-ruling “row arity STRUCTURALLY ==
//     width” law — that invariant is **operator-pending**; the top prose does
//     **not** claim current types make ragged rows unrepresentable.
//   - `csv_parse` / `csv_emit` — 🟡 deferred (Deferred (1)); `Outcome<…>`
//     seam per json.dag #3184 when bodies land.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/collection.dag, std/text.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-4.6
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.extdeps.formats.csv


import v4.std.nat { Nat }


