// carriers (`List<String>` per row, `Nat` width metadata) with explicit 🟡
// (2) trigger. Structural illegal-state unrepresentability (INVARIANTS §2)
// for rectangularity waits that ruling + any substrate it instructs (same
// class as toml.dag `NonEmptyStr` / header reconcile — tracked-not-silent).
//
// DECLARATIVE-NOW / OPERATIONS-DEFERRED-WITH-OWNER. Modeled NOW: `CsvRow`,
// `CsvDocument`, **`CsvDialect` (nullary RFC 4180 profile)**, and
// `CsvHeaderPresence`.
// DEFERRED (🟡, named owner + dissolution trigger, NEVER improvised, NEVER
// a bodiless `fn` — the frozen v2 seed rejects bodiless `fn`, DECISIONS
// PARSE-1): `csv_parse`/`csv_emit` bodies, **RFC §2 wire validation** (CRLF
// vs LF record framing policy, Unicode scalar hygiene for field text, quoted-
// field sub-machine) on std/text.dag substrate, and Char-range checks where
// the wire grammar still touches `Char` carriers. Verified pattern:
// std/collection.dag #3169 + canonical json.dag #3184.
