// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CsvDialect — **nullary witness** for the **RFC 4180 §2** wire grammar pinned
// by this file's L-2 anchor (COMMA-separated fields, DQUOTE-quoted fields with
// doubled-DQUOTE escapes — not a tunable delimiter/quote/escape parameter
// surface). Multi-profile / “Excel CSV” / TSV authorities belong in a **different**
// anchor + receipt, not silent parameterization here (P1 modeling faithfulness).
//
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / INVARIANTS P1) — 🟢 GREEN (terminal).
// Ledger — single RFC profile; additional dialects = new sum arms or sibling
// modules under operator pin, not open `Char` parameters.
type CsvDialect
  = CsvDialectRfc4180


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CsvHeaderPresence — optional header row (immutable-header `header:
// Option<Row>`). `HeaderPresent.row` is ONE logical header record.
//
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4) — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger: header row
// present vs absent are distinct shapes (same two-variant discipline as other
// optional-row sums).
type CsvHeaderPresence
  = HeaderPresent { row: CsvRow }
  | HeaderAbsent


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CsvRow — one logical record as an ordered field list. The immutable
// header names this authority `Row`; v4 declares it as `CsvRow` for grep
// stability (operator header-reconcile may alias the spelling).
//
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4) — N/A (this is a `Conj` record, not a
// sum). The row is not a recursive JSON-like value space; it is a single
// product carrying `List<String>` (A1: recursion is through `List`, not
// through `CsvRow`). **Rectangularity / arity vs `CsvDocument.width`:** no
// disposition until **pending operator csv-rectangularity ruling** (see
// modeling notes + Deferred (2)).
type CsvRow {
  fields: List<String>,
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CsvDocument — a header slot + body records + the logical field-count
// metadata `width` from the immutable scaffold header (`PositiveInt` in
// prose). Delivered `width: Nat` is the honest counting carrier (Peano
// `Nat` from std/nat.dag — the same non-negative counting discipline as
// the rest of the numeric tower); **strict positive width** (`PositiveInt`)
// is refinement-substrate operator-pending — surfaced here, not fabricated
// as a pretend `PositiveInt` type.
//
// Anchor: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4180#section-2
//
// **Rectangularity / row arity / `width` consistency:** no worker-chosen
// policy — frozen on trigger **pending operator csv-rectangularity ruling**
// (🟡 (2)); until then the `Conj` may structurally admit combinations the
// eventual ruling will classify as illegal; parse/emit bodies do not close
// that gap here (INVARIANTS §2 honesty: no false structural guarantee).
type CsvDocument {
  width: Nat,
  header: CsvHeaderPresence,
  records: List<CsvRow>,
}


